{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>וְיָדַעְתָּ כִּי לֹא וגו׳ זְכוֹר אַל תִּשְׁכַּח וגו׳.</b> It is difficult: what does it prove from what happened at the times when there were wicked ones among them, to this time — for it is possible that the righteousness in which they stand today suffices for them to inherit the land, and they can say, ״In my righteousness HaShem has brought me״? Yet the intention is this: from the fact that they saw, at the time when they were rebelling against HaShem on the way of their entry into the land, that even so they kept journeying and coming to inherit it, from this it follows that their entry is on account of the covenant of the fathers, and there is no proof from the fact that they are coming to the land that it is by their own merit that they come."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:18.419154135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}